+++ b/migration/CONVENTIONS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+# FreeMarker -> Tessera conventions for this migration (BudgetMaster)
+
+Read /work/guide.md (sections 1, 4, 6, 7) first. App module: /work/app/BudgetMasterServer.
+Templates root: BudgetMasterServer/src/main/resources/templates. Each `x/y.ftl` becomes `x/y.html`
+(same view name, so controllers keep returning the same strings). Delete the `.ftl` once its
+`.html` is written. Do NOT touch pom.xml. Never use SafeHtml.unchecked / TrustedUrl.unchecked, never
+disable CSRF/escaping, never add permitAll, never touch tests except where they assert on FreeMarker.
+
+## Already in place (read these files, they are the examples to copy)
+- `helpers/header.html`: fragments `header(title)`, `logo(page,id,classes)`, `modalConfirmDelete(...)`,
+  `showNotifications(page.notifications)`, `hint(hint, icon, actionUrl)`, `buttonLink(10 args)`,
+  `buttonSubmit(10 args)`, `buttonFlat(10 args)`, `entityIcon(icon, classes, fallbackName)`.
+  FreeMarker macro defaults do not exist in Tessera: pass every argument (defaults are listed in comments).
+- `helpers/navbar.html`: `navbar(PageContext page, String activeID)`.
+- `helpers/scripts.html`: `scripts` (no args).
+- `helpers/customSelectMacros.html`: so far only `accountIcon(page, account, accountName, classes, datasetValue)`;
+  the owner of customSelectMacros adds the other macros to this same file.
+- `helpers/colors.html` (GENERATED by migration/tools/gen_colors.py, don't edit): Tessera rejects
+  expressions in `style`. Elements with `style="color: ${x}"`/`background-color` use these fragments,
+  which switch over the app's known colors: `div|span|a(prop, color, id, classes, dataValue, Fragment content)`,
+  `iconSpan(color, icon, iconClasses, fallbackName)`, `circle(bgColor, classes, dataValue, fontColor, icon, iconClasses, fallbackName)`.
+  If you need another colour/shape, add it to gen_colors.py and re-run it (tell the lead in your report).
+- Java, package `de.deadlocker8.budgetmaster.view`:
+  - `PageContext` (model attribute **`page`** on every request, from PageContextAdvice): `page.settings`
+    (Settings entity), `page.darkTheme`, `page.categorySquare`, `page.greenTextColor`, `page.redTextColor`,
+    `page.notifications`, current account/budget, etc. Replaces FreeMarker globals
+    (`settings.isUseDarkTheme()`, `greenTextColor`, `redTextColor`, `notifications`).
+  - function namespaces: `locale.getString('key')` / `locale.getString('key', a, b)` (exact replacement for
+    FreeMarker's `locale.getString(...)`), `view.initial(s)`, `view.fontColor(item, page.darkTheme)`
+    (= `item.getFontColor(settings.isUseDarkTheme())`), `view.c(id)` (= `id?c`), `links.root()`,
+    `entityType.of('HOME')` (= `entityType.HOME`).
+  - `SpringBeans.get(SomeService.class)` for static access to beans from your own @TemplateFunctions.
+- Model attributes still provided by advices: `settings` (Settings), `build` (Build), `localizedWeekdays`,
+  `localizedMonthNames`, `categoryColors` (List<String>). REMOVED: `helpers`, `dateService`,
+  `currencyService`, `updateService`, `notifications`, `static` — anything a template got from these must
+  now come from (a) a getter on a view-safe type, (b) a controller-provided model attribute, or (c) your own
+  `@TemplateFunctions` class.
+- All `@Entity` classes and `Notification` are annotated `@TemplateView`. Annotate other classes you need
+  (add `import dev.tessera.runtime.TemplateView;` + `@TemplateView`). Records/enums need nothing.
+
+## Page skeleton (FreeMarker header/body/content macros are inlined, not fragment calls)
+```html
+<html xmlns:t="https://tessera.dev" t:import="de.deadlocker8.budgetmaster.view.PageContext, de.deadlocker8.budgetmaster.categories.Category"
+      t:params="PageContext page, List<Category> categories">
+    <head>
+        <t:block t:replace="~{helpers/header :: header('BudgetMaster - ' + locale.getString('menu.categories'))}"></t:block>
+        <link type="text/css" rel="stylesheet" t:href="@{/css/customSelect.css}"/>   <!-- was <@header.style "customSelect"/> -->
+    </head>
+    <body class="background-blue-light" t:data-theme="page.darkTheme ? 'dark'">  <!-- was <@header.body> -->
+        <t:block t:replace="~{helpers/navbar :: navbar(page, 'categories')}"></t:block>
+        <main> ...
+            <t:block t:replace="~{helpers/header :: showNotifications(page.notifications)}"></t:block> <!-- was <@header.content> -->
+            ...
+        </main>
+        <t:block t:replace="~{helpers/scripts :: scripts}"></t:block>
+        <script t:src="@{/js/categories.js}"></script>
+    </body>
+</html>
+```
+Notes:
+- `<@s.url '/x'/>` -> `@{/x}`; with variables `@{/categories/{id}/edit(id=category.ID)}`. A URL string
+  computed at runtime goes in `t:href="someString"`. The context path is `/`.
+- Getters: `category.getName()` -> `category.name`; `isX()` -> `x.isX()` or `x.x`; methods with
+  arguments or non-getter methods (`needToShowX()`, `getFontColor(bool)`) are NOT callable: add a getter,
+  a function, or a model attribute. `x?c` -> just `x` (ints print plain) or `view.c(x)` for null-safety.
+  `x??` -> `x != null`; `x?has_content` -> `!#strings.isEmpty(x)` / `!list.isEmpty()`.
+  `<#list xs as x>` -> `t:each="x, xStat : xs"`, `x?index` -> `xStat.index`, `x?counter` -> `xStat.count`.
+  `<#assign>` -> `t:with`. Macros -> `t:fragment` with typed params (no defaults; fragments see only params).
+- Old engine printed `${...}` UNescaped; Tessera escapes. Values that contained markup now come out
+  escaped: that is accepted, note it in your report.
+- `<form method="post">` gets the CSRF hidden input automatically: DELETE the explicit
+  `<input type="hidden" name="${_csrf.parameterName}" value="${_csrf.token}"/>` lines.
+- Forms: the old templates mostly write `name="..." value="${obj.x}"` by hand; keep that style
+  (`t:value="obj.x"`) unless t:field is simpler. Validation errors are read by the `validation.ftl` macros
+  from the `error` model attribute (a BindingResult?) — check how; the validation.html owner defines it.
+- Inline JS: `var x = "${foo}";` -> `var x = [[${foo}]];` (Tessera writes JSON, including the quotes).
+- Text in a page must stay the same (same whitespace-insensitive DOM). The parity tool compares the DOM
+  (whitespace, attribute order, class order, comments don't matter).
+
+## Building (shared source tree, several agents work at once)
+Never run maven in /work/app directly. Build a private copy:
+```sh
+rsync -a --delete --exclude target --exclude build /work/app/ /tmp/build-$NAME/ && \
+  cd /tmp/build-$NAME && mvn -B -q -o clean compile -pl BudgetMasterServer 2>&1 | grep -E 'error:' | sort -u
+```
+Errors from other agents' files will show up while they work: fix only yours (grep for your paths).
+Keep Java files compiling at all times (a Java syntax error blocks everyone's template checking).
+When the whole tree compiles you may run the app to look at your pages:
+`psql -h /tmp/pg -U postgres -c "create database $NAME owner budgetmaster"` then
+`java -jar /tmp/build-$NAME/BudgetMasterServer/build/2.18.2/BudgetMasterServer-v2.18.2.jar --budgetmaster.database.databaseName=$NAME --server.port=$PORT`
+(after `mvn -B -q -o package -DskipTests` in your copy); login: POST /login username=Default&password=BudgetMaster.
+The original app's recorded pages are in /work/app/migration/baseline/NN.html (requests in index.tsv,
+request list in /work/app/migration/pages.txt); the original app runs at http://localhost:8081 (do not POST to it).
